# ── Data, never committed ───────────────────────────────
# Code and data live apart: all data goes under data/, so blocking the whole
# directory is enough and no future data file can slip through. A knowledge
# base can be rebuilt from the original documentation, and its size is far
# beyond what Git is for. Back it up by copying files (see _backup/).
data/
_backup/

# In case someone builds a library outside data/.
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm

# ── Your own libraries ──────────────────────────────────
# The repository ships one worked example — datasets/EXAMPLE.toml and
# docatlas/sources/example.py — and nothing else. Which documentation you
# collect is your choice, not a default handed to everyone who clones this, so
# the datasets and adapters you write stay on your own machine.
#
# To contribute an adapter upstream, add it explicitly: git add -f <path>
datasets/*.toml
!datasets/EXAMPLE.toml
docatlas/sources/*.py
!docatlas/sources/__init__.py
!docatlas/sources/_html.py
!docatlas/sources/example.py
docatlas/knowledge/*.py
!docatlas/knowledge/__init__.py
tests/test_source_adapters.py

# ── Runtime ─────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# ── Editors / OS ────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Data location and default library chosen at install time; one per machine.
.docatlas-local.toml

# Internal test walkthrough, not published.
测试流.md

# One-off architecture review from before the rename; it still contains
# absolute paths from the author's machine. Kept locally, not published.
ARCHITECTURE_REVIEW.md
